 (Reduced) tillage;
 Specific crop rotations / catch crops and crop residue management;
 N immobilization via addition of organic biological waste and crop residues: type of organic biological waste, application method, environmental circumstances, dose, etc.;
 Temporary and permanent grassland and grazing vs mowing;
 Peaty permanent grasslands in the Polder area and its soil and water management;
 Land use change (including conversion of grassland to arable land).
